        "file": "app/proc-info/main.c",
        "start_line": 1615,
        "end_line": 1616,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "EEPROM length from driver not bounded by 1024-byte stack buffer",
        "explanation": "eeprom_info.length is taken from module_info.eeprom_len, which is supplied by the PMD, and the driver then writes that many bytes into the fixed 1024-byte stack buffer bytes_eeprom. If a driver reports a larger length, the stack buffer overflows. The code never checks the length against EEPROM_DUMP_CHUNKSIZE.",
        "suggestion": "Check module_info.eeprom_len against sizeof(bytes_eeprom). Return an error or read in chunks if it is larger. Also memset eeprom_info before use.",
        "evidence": "eeprom_info.length = module_info.eeprom_len;",
        "confidence": 0.5,
        "id": "3806d63a48af",
